Buffer numbers (microstep 1): **capacity 720 frames**, **capture cadence one frame per
simulation tick (1/120 s)**, **playback cadence one index per rendered frame at 1/60 s**
(so a point replays at half the speed it was played — the reference's own ratio), frame
payload the reference's `serveSide/serveCourt/activePlayerKey` + 17 ball fields + 4 pads ×
10 fields. At ~1.1-1.3 KB per frame by JSON encoding (the audit prints the measured
value), the whole ring is on the order of **0.8-1.0 MB** at the shipped bound — the
"buffer memory" line of the ticket's failure list.

