## 12. The runs, executed — finalize closure (2026-09-17, integration owner)

**State: the runs owed in §9 are done; §10's blockers are closed.** Registry: the whole pack was
re-run serially (one Godot process at a time, `pgrep -x Godot` guard) — **32/32 green**,
`evidence/uir-finalize/ui-audit-sweep.json`, tree digest `1256f5f1d7200437`, stable; this suite
**PASS 166/166, exit 0, 0 `SCRIPT ERROR`** (log `evidence/uir-finalize/runs/replay_audit.log`),
slice **PASS 342/342**, demo **293/293**.

- **The seam landed** in `godot/game/match_controller.gd`: `start_replay()` (refuses null /
  finished / already-up / <2 frames; records and clears the pause), `stop_replay()` (idempotent;
  restores the recorded pause), `replay_active()`, `replay_progress()` = `(index+1)/total` clamped,
  `replay_index()`, `replay_frame_count()`, `replay_was_paused()`, the `replay_finished` signal.
  Playback runs inside `apply_frame` (rung before the pause check): one frame per `1/60` s of
  rendered delta, frame applied → `_sync_views()` → restore. ESC's replay rung sits FIRST, outside
  the card arm; `r` toggles in play and is refused while the card is up.
- **The pause flag split (§3.4 / §10.2) — picked and wired**: the playback reading feeds
  `set_replay_active` (ESC's step 0 can never be stale), and a new availability reading
  `set_replay_available(_replay_can_start())` gates the card's entry, fed on every pause edge and
  every entry/exit. The card's entry is pressable exactly while a playback can start and runs
  `start_replay()` — the reference's card entry hides the card and toggles (`js/main.js:2238-2241`);
  it no longer routes through `toggle_replay()`'s paused refusal.
- **One audit correction, with its citation** (`replay/the_restarted_record_is_not_the_old_one`):
  the ball-triple inequality it asserted is impossible under the reference — the forced point end
  re-runs `prepare_serve` with the serve side unchanged (`sim.gd:643-676`), so the fresh record's
  first frame IS the same canonical serve state the match opened on, byte for byte. Replaced with
  the array-identity proof (the held reference must stop growing because the reset replaces the
  array, `sim.gd:248`); the failure mode the check exists for (no reset) still fails it.
- **The two overlay contract fixes** (§4, landed with this closure): `bind_seam()` attaches only
  (the caller's next `refresh()` is the first read), and `refresh()` with no seam hides.
